 "title": "$1,000 crossed a border. No money moved 🤝",
 "description": "Hawala, explained: a sender in New York gives a broker cash and a code word, a second broker in Lahore pays the cousin from her own cash, and only a debt is left between the brokers, settled later with goods or transfers the other way. Cheap, fast and built on trust: licensed in some countries, illegal in others (including India), and, as a UN study found, also used by criminals. A documentary explainer, not advice.\n\nSources: Corporate Finance Institute (Hawala); ClearTax (Hawala in India, FEMA); UNODC (2023) on hawala and organised crime; FATF report on underground banking and hawala (Sept 2026).",
